# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_namespace_edge_precision.py" "NAMESPACE EDGE PRECISION GATE: PASS" "namespace-edge precision: uncorroborated C#/Go namespace import edges are KEPT as \`imports\` (recall-safe), demotion proven NOT safe" "namespace-edge precision INVESTIGATION + RECALL GUARD: the extractor resolves a C# \`using A.B.C;\` (_resolve_csharp_ns) and a Go package import (_resolve_go_pkg) to EVERY .cs/.go file in the namespace DIRECTORY -- one \`using\` => N \`imports\` edges (measured: jellyfin 94k, hugo 12k). Java is UNAFFECTED (explicit import = one file, wildcard = nothing; gson/okhttp = 0 fan-out edges). HYPOTHESIS: an UNCORROBORATED namespace edge (F imports G but \`calls\` no symbol G defines) is spurious, so demoting it cuts cry-wolf recall-free. MEASURED co-change (engine bar support>=3 lift>=2 vs random same-lang baseline): the uncorroborated signal is REPO-DEPENDENT -- at baseline in jellyfin (x0.2) / gin (x0.2), but ABOVE baseline in CliWrap (x2.6) and hugo (x1.7). The RECALL-DECISIVE sole-carrier test (mirrors PR #252): of uncorroborated edges that DO co-change, how many are the SOLE structural carrier? CliWrap 12/12, hugo 31/31, jellyfin 27/31, gin 1/1, gorm 32/32 -- almost ALL sole-carrier real couplings (hugo: filecache_config_test<->filecache_config co=5/5 lift 243). WHY: the call-corroboration test is INCOMPLETE -- F can use G via a constructor/type/field/interface/unresolved-call with no \`calls\` edge, so \`uncorroborated\` conflates \`uses nothing\` (spurious) with \`uses G but resolver missed it\` (legitimate); fan-out WIDTH does not separate them either (hugo width-21+ still x1.3, CliWrap width-2 x2.3). VERDICT: demoting uncorroborated namespace edges is NOT recall-safe (would silently lose 75/107 sole-carrier real couplings across the 5 repos) -- a valid HONEST negative, identical in shape to PR #252's call-edge finding. Implemented NOTHING that demotes them. This gate PINS that the namespace import edge (corroborated AND uncorroborated) stays a NORMAL \`imports\` edge -- never dropped, never minted into a non-ingestible (silently-dropped) kind -- so a future \`precision fix\` that drops/demotes the uncorroborated edge in the extractor FAILS here; plus the Java no-fan-out control. Hermetic synthetic C#/Java graph; content-free (edge kinds + paths + symbol names)" "namespace-edge precision: the uncorroborated C#/Go namespace import edge is recall-safely KEPT as \`imports\` (never dropped, never minted into a non-ingestible kind); demotion proven NOT recall-safe by sole-carrier co-change measurement; Java no-fan-out control intact" 20
